# Testing Standards

Stack: **Vitest + Testing Library** (`skills/testing.md`).

## What must get tests

- Pure utilities (`lib/format`, `lib/utils`, error helpers)
- Schemas / parsers with branching
- Hooks with non-trivial logic
- Critical guards (e.g. protected routes) when changed

## What usually skips unit tests

- Pure presentational layout sections (validate via quality gate + responsive QA)
- Static marketing copy

## Patterns

```ts
// Prefer behavior over implementation details
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react'
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest'
```

- Use accessible queries (`getByRole`, `getByLabelText`) first
- Keep tests deterministic; no network without mocks
- Run `npm run test` as part of the quality gate after logic changes

E2E (`test:e2e`) is a placeholder until Playwright/Cypress is configured — do not invent a second test runner without asking.
